  "user_solution": "/*\n\ntransforms this wide-format into long format with one row per job-phase combination.\nThe output must have four columns: \n`job_id`, \n`run_timestamp`, \n`phase_name`, \n`duration_sec`.\n\nMapping:\n`init_duration_sec` to phase_name='initialization', \n`processing_duration_sec` to phase_name='processing',\n `finalization_duration_sec` to phase_name='finalization'.\n\nInclude rows where the duration is NULL (some phases may not have recorded durations).\nOrder the result by `job_id` ASC, then `phase_name` ASC.\n\n*/\n\nSELECT\n    job_id,\n    run_timestamp,\n    'initialization' AS phase_name,\n    init_duration_sec AS duration_sec\nFROM job_execution_summary\n\n\nUNION ALL\n\nSELECT\n    job_id,\n    run_timestamp,\n    'processing' AS phase_name,\n    processing_duration_sec AS duration_sec\nFROM job_execution_summary\n\n\nUNION ALL\n\nSELECT\n    job_id,\n    run_timestamp,\n    'finalization' AS phase_name,\n    finalization_duration_sec AS duration_sec\nFROM job_execution_summary\n\n\nORDER BY 1, 3;\n\n\n",
  "solved_at": "2026-05-07T08:19:46.118598"
